!! Status module: the summary card and the top bar's live readouts.
!!
!! Owns everything that answers "what is the system doing right now": the aggregate "N rooms calling for heat" title, the frost-protection rule, the summary card, the second row of the top bar (date, profile, outside reading, frost badge), the demand flame, and the system name under the heartbeat. The shell hands it a snapshot of the map and it paints.
!!
!! Loaded by shell.allspeak at boot, after the top bar exists. Its clock tick runs here too: the card and the banner both show the time, and neither changes when a map does, so the tick is part of this module rather than the shell.
!!
!! Why it is a module: all of it is one transformation — rooms and a few map fields in, DOM out — and none of it mutates anything the shell owns. The shell used to recompute the aggregates in five places and then remember to repaint the card after each; now there is one `paint` message and no state to keep in step.
!!
!! The frost rule is the one thing worth carrying across the boundary: the controller may set `frostActive` itself, and when it does not, the module derives it from the trigger, the outside temperature and whether any room is calling. Both the card's badge and the banner's snowflake read the same computed flag, which is why they cannot disagree.
!!
!! Messages, as a dict with `action`:
!!
!!   `mount` — the full home has just rendered the summary card (the shell renders the layout). Attach its elements, then paint from this snapshot.
!!
!!   `paint` — a snapshot changed: a map push, a view switch, a room command. Paint everything that is on screen.
!!
!!   `unmount` — the card has gone (the simple home replaced the column). Stop painting card elements until the next mount.
!!
!! Every message is fire-and-forget. A send that waited would park the shell and take this program's single reply slot, which is how a map push gets dropped.

	script Status

	div SummaryTitle
	div SummaryOutside
	div SummaryOutsideFrost
	div SummaryToday
	div SummaryProfileName
	div SummaryChip
	div SummaryChipIcon
	div SummaryDot
	div TopBarDate
	div TopBarProfileName
	div TopBarOutsideBlock
	div TopBarOutside
	div TopBarOutsideFrost
	div HeartbeatFlame
	div SystemId

	variable StatusMessage
	variable StatusAction
	variable SummaryMounted

	variable RoomsIn
	variable RoomCountIn
	variable OutsideTempIn
	variable OutsideSensorIn
	variable FrostTriggerIn
	variable FrostActiveIn
	variable RequestRelayIn
	variable SystemNameIn
	variable ActiveProfileNameIn

	variable HeatingCount
	variable HeatingNames
	variable OutsideText
	variable TitleText
	variable FrostActive
	variable DemandOn
	variable SummaryTitleHeat
	variable LoopI
	variable CurRoom
	variable RName
	variable Tcalling
	variable OutsideTempTenths
	variable FrostTriggerTenths

	variable DayNames
	variable MonthNames
	variable DayName
	variable MonthName
	variable DateD
	variable DateDN
	variable DateM
	variable DateH
	variable DateN
	variable DateClock
	variable ClockText
!! @hash 5169fc25
!!!

!! Boot: claim the top bar's readouts, start the clock, then park for snapshots.
!!
!! The top bar is rendered by the shell before this module loads, so its elements exist to attach. `SystemId` is claimed here too: the shell sets its first text ("…" or "Reconnecting…") while the connection is still being made, and this module replaces it with the system's name once a map arrives.
!!
!! The clock tick starts here rather than in the shell because it repaints two cells that both belong to this module.
BootStatus:
	attach TopBarDate to `top-bar-date`
	attach TopBarProfileName to `top-bar-profile-name`
	attach TopBarOutsideBlock to `top-bar-outside-block`
	attach TopBarOutside to `top-bar-outside`
	attach TopBarOutsideFrost to `top-bar-outside-frost`
	attach HeartbeatFlame to `top-bar-demand-flame`
	attach SystemId to `top-bar-system-id`

	put `[]` into DayNames
	set element 0 of DayNames to `Sun`
	set element 1 of DayNames to `Mon`
	set element 2 of DayNames to `Tue`
	set element 3 of DayNames to `Wed`
	set element 4 of DayNames to `Thu`
	set element 5 of DayNames to `Fri`
	set element 6 of DayNames to `Sat`
	put `[]` into MonthNames
	set element 0 of MonthNames to `Jan`
	set element 1 of MonthNames to `Feb`
	set element 2 of MonthNames to `Mar`
	set element 3 of MonthNames to `Apr`
	set element 4 of MonthNames to `May`
	set element 5 of MonthNames to `Jun`
	set element 6 of MonthNames to `Jul`
	set element 7 of MonthNames to `Aug`
	set element 8 of MonthNames to `Sep`
	set element 9 of MonthNames to `Oct`
	set element 10 of MonthNames to `Nov`
	set element 11 of MonthNames to `Dec`

	fork to ClockTick
	on message go to HandleStatus
	release parent
	stop
!! @hash 8d24fd89
!!!
!! Message handler: unpack the snapshot, then mount, paint or unmount.
HandleStatus:
	put the message into StatusMessage
	put property `action` of StatusMessage into StatusAction
	if StatusAction is not `unmount`
	begin
		put property `rooms` of StatusMessage into RoomsIn
		put property `roomCount` of StatusMessage into RoomCountIn
		put property `outsideTemp` of StatusMessage into OutsideTempIn
		put property `outsideSensor` of StatusMessage into OutsideSensorIn
		put property `frostTrigger` of StatusMessage into FrostTriggerIn
		put property `frostActive` of StatusMessage into FrostActiveIn
		put property `requestRelay` of StatusMessage into RequestRelayIn
		put property `systemName` of StatusMessage into SystemNameIn
		put property `activeProfileName` of StatusMessage into ActiveProfileNameIn
	end
	if StatusAction is `mount`
	begin
		gosub to AttachSummaryCard
		gosub to PaintStatus
	end
	if StatusAction is `paint` gosub to PaintStatus
	if StatusAction is `unmount` clear SummaryMounted
	stop
!! @hash 603cb77c
!!!
!! Attach the summary card's own elements after the shell has rendered its layout into the main column.
!!
!! Called on every `mount`, because a view switch clears the main column and the next full home renders a fresh card — the handles from the previous one point at elements that are gone.
AttachSummaryCard:
	attach SummaryTitle to `summary-title`
	attach SummaryOutside to `summary-outside`
	attach SummaryOutsideFrost to `summary-outside-frost`
	attach SummaryToday to `summary-today`
	attach SummaryProfileName to `summary-profile-name`
	attach SummaryChip to `summary-chip`
	attach SummaryChipIcon to `summary-chip-icon`
	attach SummaryDot to `summary-chip-dot`
	set SummaryMounted
	return
!! @hash bef2b784
!!!
!! Recompute the aggregates and repaint everything this module owns.
!!
!! The card is painted only while it is mounted; the banner and the flame live in the top bar and are always there, so they are painted in both views. In the full view the shell hides the banner's row with CSS, and in the simple view it hides the card by not building it — either way the paint is harmless where it is not seen.
PaintStatus:
	gosub to ComputeSummaryStats
	if SummaryMounted gosub to PaintSummary
	gosub to PaintBannerInfo
	return
!! @hash 4c0a2e09
!!!
!! Walk the rooms in the snapshot and recompute the card's aggregates.
!!
!! Sets HeatingCount, HeatingNames, OutsideText, TitleText and FrostActive. `FrostActiveIn` is the controller's own `frostActive` flag, when it sets one — it knows things the UI does not, such as demand-relay state. Otherwise frost protection is derived: active when a trigger is set, the outside temperature is at or below it, and no rooms are calling.
!!
!! Title picks one of four messages: "Frost protection active" (overrides everything), "Nothing calling for heat" (idle), "<Room> is calling for heat" (single), or "<N> rooms calling for heat" with comma-joined names (multi).
ComputeSummaryStats:
	put 0 into HeatingCount
	put empty into HeatingNames
	put 0 into LoopI
	while LoopI is less than RoomCountIn
	begin
		put element LoopI of RoomsIn into CurRoom
		put property `name` of CurRoom into RName
		put property `calling` of CurRoom into Tcalling
		if Tcalling is `yes`
		begin
			increment HeatingCount
			if HeatingNames is empty put RName into HeatingNames
			else put HeatingNames cat `, ` cat RName into HeatingNames
		end
		increment LoopI
	end

	put `—` into OutsideText
	if OutsideTempIn is not empty put OutsideTempIn cat `°C` into OutsideText

	clear FrostActive
	if FrostActiveIn is `yes` set FrostActive
	else
	begin
		if FrostTriggerIn is not empty
		begin
			if OutsideTempIn is not empty
			begin
				if HeatingCount is 0
				begin
					put OutsideTempIn scale 10 into OutsideTempTenths
					put FrostTriggerIn scale 10 into FrostTriggerTenths
					if OutsideTempTenths is not greater than FrostTriggerTenths set FrostActive
				end
			end
		end
	end

	if FrostActive
	begin
		put `Frost protection active` into TitleText
	end
	else if HeatingCount is 0
	begin
		put `Nothing calling for heat` into TitleText
	end
	else if HeatingCount is 1
	begin
		put HeatingNames cat ` is calling for heat` into TitleText
	end
	else
	begin
		put HeatingCount cat ` rooms calling for heat` into TitleText
	end
	gosub to PaintDemandFlame
	return
!! @hash 7c10c4e0
!!!
!! Push the aggregates into the summary card and keep the card's own live fields current.
!!
!! The title takes the same accent colour as a room name while any room is calling; frost protection is its own state, not a heat call-out. The date, profile name and system name depend on live data, so they are refreshed here rather than at startup. The frost badge in the outside row toggles inline-block against none, and the chip swaps heat for neutral on HeatingCount.
PaintSummary:
	set the content of SummaryTitle to TitleText
	set the content of SummaryOutside to OutsideText
	clear SummaryTitleHeat
	if HeatingCount is greater than 0 set SummaryTitleHeat
	if FrostActive clear SummaryTitleHeat
	if SummaryTitleHeat set style `color` of SummaryTitle to `var(--color-accent)`
	else set style `color` of SummaryTitle to `var(--color-text-primary)`

	gosub to FormatTodayString
	set the content of SummaryToday to ClockText

	if ActiveProfileNameIn is not empty set the content of SummaryProfileName to ActiveProfileNameIn
!	The first map ends the "Reconnecting…" state shown by the first-map
!	watchdog. A system with no name gets the blank loading mark back rather
!	than leaving the recovery text there for ever.
	if SystemNameIn is not empty set the content of SystemId to SystemNameIn
	if SystemNameIn is empty set the content of SystemId to `…`

	if FrostActive set style `display` of SummaryOutsideFrost to `inline-block`
	else set style `display` of SummaryOutsideFrost to `none`

	if HeatingCount is 0
	begin
		set style `background` of SummaryChip to `var(--color-chip-neutral-bg)`
		set style `background-color` of SummaryChipIcon to `var(--color-text-muted)`
		set style `display` of SummaryDot to `none`
	end
	else
	begin
		set style `background` of SummaryChip to `var(--color-chip-heat-bg)`
		set style `background-color` of SummaryChipIcon to `var(--color-chip-heat-fg)`
		set style `display` of SummaryDot to `block`
	end
	return
!! @hash 5446f3f6
!!!
!! Paint the banner's second row: date and time, active profile name, outside reading, frost badge.
!!
!! The profile name is always shown. The outside half appears only when an outside thermometer is configured; without one the Profile button is the profile editor's entry point alone. A configured sensor with no reading yet shows an em dash rather than a misleading zero. The frost snowflake follows FrostActive — the controller's flag if present, otherwise outside at or below the trigger with no room calling.
PaintBannerInfo:
	gosub to FormatTodayString
	set the content of TopBarDate to ClockText
	if ActiveProfileNameIn is not empty set the content of TopBarProfileName to ActiveProfileNameIn
	else set the content of TopBarProfileName to `—`
	if OutsideSensorIn is not empty
	begin
		set style `display` of TopBarOutsideBlock to `flex`
		if OutsideTempIn is empty set the content of TopBarOutside to `—`
		else set the content of TopBarOutside to OutsideTempIn
	end
	else set style `display` of TopBarOutsideBlock to `none`
	if FrostActive set style `display` of TopBarOutsideFrost to `block`
	else set style `display` of TopBarOutsideFrost to `none`
	return
!! @hash 12e650ee
!!!
!! Show the flame beside the heartbeat dot while the demand relay is on.
!!
!! The map names the demand relay but does not say whether it is firing, so the module derives that from the two things the controller fires it for: any room calling for heat, and frost protection, which fires it with no room calling. A system with no request relay has nothing to report, so the flame stays away however many rooms heat on their own valves.
PaintDemandFlame:
	clear DemandOn
	if RequestRelayIn is not empty
	begin
		if HeatingCount is greater than 0 set DemandOn
		if FrostActive set DemandOn
	end
	if DemandOn set style `visibility` of HeartbeatFlame to `visible`
	else set style `visibility` of HeartbeatFlame to `hidden`
	return
!! @hash bbf43f81
!!!
!! Build today's date and the current time as "Tue 20 Oct 09:19" into ClockText.
!!
!! Uses the day and month lookup tables and the browser's own date keywords — this runtime has no `datime` — so ClockTick can refresh it between map pushes. Both time fields are zero-padded.
FormatTodayString:
	put the day into DateD
	put the day number into DateDN
	put the month into DateM
	put element DateD of DayNames into DayName
	put element DateM of MonthNames into MonthName
	put the hour into DateH
	put the minute into DateN
	if DateH is less than 10 put `0` cat DateH into DateClock
	else put `` cat DateH into DateClock
	if DateN is less than 10 put DateClock cat `:0` cat DateN into DateClock
	else put DateClock cat `:` cat DateN into DateClock
	put DayName cat ` ` cat DateDN cat ` ` cat MonthName cat ` ` cat DateClock into ClockText
	return
!! @hash 431fcbc3
!!!
!! Keep the displayed time current between map pushes.
!!
!! Forked at boot. The controller only pushes a full map when state changes, so without this the displayed time would freeze until the next temperature or relay change. Only the date cells are repainted, which keeps the tick cheap.
ClockTick:
	while true
	begin
		wait 30 seconds
		gosub to FormatTodayString
		set the content of TopBarDate to ClockText
		if SummaryMounted set the content of SummaryToday to ClockText
	end
!! @hash 5e6d57bb
!!!
